<iscomment>
    The product strip shared by all three sponsored brand formats.

    Each slide is a direct child of .ts-sb-carousel, which is what Slick expects, and wraps a
    Tile-Show remote include so the tiles match the ones in the product grid. carouselTile is
    passed for the same reason the Einstein carousel passes it: it switches the tile to its
    carousel styling. isSponsored is deliberately omitted so the tiles carry no "featured"
    badge, since the disclosure label sits on the row instead.

    Expects the "sbRow" page variable.
</iscomment>

<div class="ts-sb-products">
    <div class="ts-sb-carousel">
        <isloop items="${sbRow.products}" var="sbPid" status="sbProductLoop">
            <div class="ts-sb-slide">
                <div class="ts-sb-product" data-ts-sb-product data-pid="${sbPid}">
                    <isinclude url="${URLUtils.url('Tile-Show', 'pid', sbPid, 'swatches', true, 'badges', true, 'icons', true, 'ratings', false, 'pricing', true, 'name', true, 'showQuickView', false, 'carouselTile', true, 'cgid', pdict.request.querystring.cgid, 'origin', 'sponsoredBrand', 'tilesLoopCount', sbProductLoop.index)}" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </isloop>
    </div>
</div>
